// The node-walk select delivered every scrutinee update to every
// guarded arm's binds before ticking the guard, whether or not the
// arm's shape admitted the value. The checker narrows the binds by
// that shape, so `rows` here is Array<i64> and the guard fuses to that
// type, and the Null the `null as _` arm had already claimed arrived
// in it as a kernel param of the wrong shape (now a panic; then a
// logged mismatch treated as bottom). The select itself node-walks
// (a nullable scrutinee's bind predicate is not scalar), which is what
// leaves the guard to fuse on its own. Found by the admin TUI suite,
// 390 mismatches per run. The bind is now gated on the arm's shape.
{let step = i64:0; step <- select step {s if s < i64:6 => s + i64:1, _ => never()};
 let q: [Array<i64>, null] = null;
 q <- select step {i64:1 => [i64:7, i64:8], i64:2 => null, i64:3 => [], i64:4 => [i64:9], i64:5 => null, _ => never()};
 select q {null as _ => i64:0, rows if array::len(rows) == i64:0 => i64:1, rows => rows[i64:0]$}}
